#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Partial Differential Equation (PDE) solver presented here is part of our"
" Quantum Innovative Computing Kit (QUICK) platform (QUICK-PDE), and is "
"packaged as a Qiskit Function. With the QUICK-PDE function, you can solve "
"domain-specific partial differential equations on IBM Quantum QPUs. This "
"function is based on the algorithm described in [ColibriTD's H-DES "
"description paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01130). This algorithm can "
"solve complex multi-physics problems, starting with Computational Fluid "
"Dynamics (CFD) and Materials Deformation (MD), and other use cases coming "
"soon.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Partial Differential Equation (PDE) solver na ipinapakita dito ay bahagi"
" ng aming Quantum Innovative Computing Kit (QUICK) platform (QUICK-PDE), at "
"nakabalot bilang isang Qiskit Function. Sa pamamagitan ng QUICK-PDE "
"function, maaari kang maglutas ng domain-specific partial differential "
"equations sa IBM Quantum QPUs. Ang function na ito ay nakabatay sa algorithm"
" na inilalarawan sa [papel ng paglalarawan ng H-DES ng "
"ColibriTD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01130). Kaya ng algorithm na ito na "
"harapin ang mga kumplikadong multi-physics na problema, simula sa "
"Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) at Materials Deformation (MD), at may mga"
" karagdagang use case na paparating pa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To tackle the differential equations, the trial solutions are encoded as "
"linear combinations of orthogonal functions (typically Chebyshev "
"polynomials, and more specifically $2^n$ of them where $n$ is the number of "
"qubits encoding your function), parametrized by the angles of a Variable "
"Quantum Circuit (VQC). The ansatz generates a state encoding the function, "
"which is evaluated by observables whose combinations allow for evaluating "
"the function at all points. You can then evaluate the loss function in which"
" the differential equations are encoded, and fine-tune the angles in a "
"hybrid loop, as shown in the following. The trial solutions get gradually "
"closer to the actual solutions until you reach a satisfactory result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para harapin ang mga differential equations, ang mga trial solution ay naka-"
"encode bilang linear combinations ng mga orthogonal function (karaniwang "
"Chebyshev polynomials, at mas partikular na $2^n$ sa kanila kung saan ang "
"$n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit na nag-e-encode ng iyong function), na may "
"parameter na mga anggulo ng isang Variable Quantum Circuit (VQC). Ang ansatz"
" ay bumubuo ng isang estado na nag-e-encode ng function, na sinusuri ng mga "
"observable na ang kombinasyon nito ay nagbibigay-daan sa pag-evaluate ng "
"function sa lahat ng punto. Maaari kang mag-evaluate ng loss function kung "
"saan naka-encode ang mga differential equations, at i-fine-tune ang mga "
"anggulo sa isang hybrid loop, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod. Ang mga "
"trial solution ay unti-unting lumalapit sa mga aktwal na solusyon hanggang "
"sa makamit mo ang kasiya-siyang resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Workflow of the QUICK-PDE function](/docs/images/guides/colibritd-"
"equation-solver/diagram.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Daloy ng trabaho ng QUICK-PDE function](/docs/images/guides/colibritd-"
"equation-solver/diagram.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to this hybrid loop, you can also chain together different "
"optimizers. This is useful when you want a global optimizer to find a good "
"set of angles, and then a more fine-tuned optimizer to follow a gradient to "
"the best set of neighboring angles. In the case of computational fluid "
"dynamics (CFD), the default optimization sequence produces the best results "
"- but in the case of material deformation (MD), while the default provides "
"good results, you can configure it further for problem-specific benefits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod sa hybrid loop na ito, maaari ka ring mag-chain ng iba't ibang "
"optimizer. Ito ay kapaki-pakinabang kapag gusto mong gamitin ang isang "
"global optimizer para mahanap ang magandang set ng mga anggulo, at "
"pagkatapos ay isang mas pinong optimizer para sundan ang gradient patungo sa"
" pinakamahusay na set ng kalapit na mga anggulo. Sa kaso ng computational "
"fluid dynamics (CFD), ang default na optimization sequence ay nagbibigay ng "
"pinakamahusay na resulta — ngunit sa kaso ng material deformation (MD), "
"habang nagbibigay ng magandang resulta ang default, maaari mo itong "
"i-configure pa para sa mga benepisyong partikular sa problema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note for each variable of the function, we specify number of qubits (which "
"you can play with). By stacking 10 identical circuits and evaluating the 10 "
"identical observables on different qubits throughout one big circuit, you "
"can noise-mitigate within the CMA optimization process, relying on the noise"
" learner method, and significantly reduce the number of shots needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na para sa bawat variable ng function, tinutukoy natin ang bilang ng"
" mga qubit (na maaari mong baguhin). Sa pag-stack ng 10 magkaparehong "
"circuit at pag-evaluate ng 10 magkaparehong observable sa iba't ibang qubit "
"sa buong isang malaking circuit, maaari kang mag-noise-mitigate sa loob ng "
"proseso ng CMA optimization, umaasa sa noise learner method, at makabuluhang"
" mabawasan ang bilang ng mga shot na kailangan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Computational fluid dynamics {#computational-fluid-dynamics}"
msgstr "Computational fluid dynamics {#computational-fluid-dynamics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The inviscid Burgers' equation, models flowing non-viscous fluids as "
"follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang inviscid Burgers' equation ay nagmo-modelo ng daloy ng mga di-malapot na"
" likido tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0,$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0,$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$u$ represents the fluid speed field. This use-case has a temporal boundary "
"condition: you can select the initial condition and then allow the system to"
" relax. Currently, the only accepted initial conditions are linear "
"functions: $ax + b$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $u$ ay kumakatawan sa field ng bilis ng likido. Ang use case na ito ay "
"may temporal na boundary condition: maaari kang pumili ng initial condition "
"at hayaan ang sistema na mag-relax. Sa kasalukuyan, ang mga tanging "
"tinatanggap na initial condition ay mga linear function: $ax + b$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The arguments for CFD's differential equations are on a fixed grid, as "
"follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga argumento para sa mga differential equation ng CFD ay nasa isang "
"fixed grid, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$t$ is between 0 and 0.95 with 30 sample points. $x$ is between 0 and 0.95 "
"with a step size of 0.2375.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $t$ ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 0.95 na may 30 sample point. Ang $x$ ay nasa"
" pagitan ng 0 at 0.95 na may step size na 0.2375.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Material deformation {#material-deformation}"
msgstr "Material Deformation {#material-deformation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This use case focuses on hypoelastic deformation with the one-dimensional "
"tensile test, in which a bar fixed in space is pulled at its other "
"extremity. We describe the problem as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang use case na ito ay nakatuon sa hypoelastic deformation na may one-"
"dimensional tensile test, kung saan ang isang bar na nakapirmi sa espasyo ay"
" hinihila sa kabilang dulo nito. Inilalarawan namin ang problema tulad ng "
"sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$u' - \\frac{\\sigma}{3K} - "
"\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\epsilon_0\\left(\\frac{\\sigma'}{\\sigma_0\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^n"
" = 0$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$u' - \\frac{\\sigma}{3K} - "
"\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\epsilon_0\\left(\\frac{\\sigma'}{\\sigma_0\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^n"
" = 0$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\sigma' - b = 0,$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\sigma' - b = 0,$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$K$ represents the bulk modulus of the material being stretched, $n$ the "
"exponent of a power law, $b$ the force per unit mass, $\\epsilon_0$ the "
"proportional stress limit, $\\sigma_0$ the proportional strain limit, $u$ "
"the stress function, and $\\sigma$ the strain function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $K$ ay kumakatawan sa bulk modulus ng materyal na iniuunat, ang $n$ ang "
"exponent ng isang power law, ang $b$ ang puwersa bawat unit mass, ang "
"$\\epsilon_0$ ang proportional stress limit, ang $\\sigma_0$ ang "
"proportional strain limit, ang $u$ ang stress function, at ang $\\sigma$ ang"
" strain function.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The considered bar is of unitary length. This use-case has a boundary "
"condition for surface stress $t$, or the amount of work needed to stretch "
"the bar.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isinasaalang-alang na bar ay may unitary na haba. Ang use case na ito ay"
" may boundary condition para sa surface stress $t$, o ang dami ng trabahong "
"kailangan para maunat ang bar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The arguments for MD's differential equations are on a fixed grid, as "
"follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga argumento para sa mga differential equation ng MD ay nasa isang "
"fixed grid, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$x$ is between 0 and 1 with a step size of 0.04.\n"
msgstr "Ang $x$ ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 1 na may step size na 0.04.\n"

